# lightpipe.mac — parametric light-pipe scaffold: 4 K Planck emitter into the bore.
#
# bbrsimLightPipe uses its own copy of the test-world Planck emitter
# (LightPipePrimaryGeneratorAction). Its test-world default box (1x20x20 mm
# centred at x = -50 mm) overlaps the tube wall, which starts at x = -50 mm
# with a 5 mm bore, so photons would be created inside the copper. Place a
# 1x7x7 mm box centred at x = -51 mm instead: the emitting face is at
# x = -50.5 mm, 0.5 mm upstream of the aperture, and its corners sit at
# r = 4.95 mm, inside the bore.
#
# Validate:
#   conda run -n bbrsim python <repo>/validation/check_invariants.py output/bbr.root
#
# Regression input: validation/Scripts/run_regression.sh runs this macro as
# case lp, and validation/Scripts/drift_guards.sh pins its command lines. Change
# them only together with the validators, then update the pin.
/run/verbose 0
/event/verbose 0
/tracking/verbose 0
/bbr/thermal/emitterCenter -51 0 0 mm
/bbr/thermal/emitterSize 1 7 7 mm
/run/initialize
/run/beamOn 50000
